Skip the public fallback nameservers when explicit nameservers are given.

On a host whose /etc/resolv.conf lists only loopback resolvers, resolvconf.New
appends 8.8.8.8 and 8.8.4.4 even when the caller passes explicit nameservers
with KeepHostServers, which is how libpod, the rootless netns, and buildah's
`podman build` pass the pasta and slirp4netns DNS forwarder. Containers then query Google DNS next to the
forwarder that reaches the host's own resolver.

Upstream issue: https://github.com/podman-container-tools/container-libs/issues/43

